# Intent: Game packs installed in the asset store (owner decision 17; the first consumer of SF90, design installed-set.md G3 step 1) join the games list and start like the built-in games: up to 8 packs of kind game, store slot n is games slot 8 + n. Each is copied from the store the first time it is asked for (the store checked its hash; mg_parse checks the pack), kept in PSRAM until the store changes and no game runs, and left out when its id is a built-in game's, so the store can never shadow a built-in. The saved scores of an installed pack are read from the unit's score store the first time its row is needed. The seven built-in games and the grid games are unchanged; with the store off the installed slots are simply empty.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_games.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: on a nofont or lean image install a signed game pack of kind game with self.assets.install, data and commit; self.game.list shows it with kind installed; self.game.start with its id plays it; its best score survives a restart; self.assets.remove makes it leave the list; a pack named like a built-in is not listed.
# Kconfig: none (needs MAIPAI_ASSET_STORE to have anything to list)
# Memory cost: nothing while no pack is installed; each installed pack is a PSRAM copy of its size (at most 16,384 bytes, 8 packs at most: 131,072 bytes) once the games list or a game asks for it; 8 more score entries (about 160 bytes) in internal RAM; flash about 1.2 KB (estimate).

